# Design System Architecture

## Layers
| Layer | Lives in | May use | Must not use |
|---|---|---|---|
| Primitive tokens | `tokens/tokens.json` → `primitive` | raw values (hex, px) | references |
| Semantic tokens | `tokens/tokens.json` → `semantic` | `{primitive.*}` references | raw values |
| Primitives | `src/components/primitives/` | semantic CSS variables | `--primitive-*`, raw values |
| Components | `src/components/` | primitives, semantic variables | fetch, stores, formatting |
| Screens | `src/screens/` | components | new styling beyond layout |

Dependencies point down only. A component never imports a screen. A primitive never imports a component.

## Token file shape
- Every leaf has `$value` and `$type` (`color`, `dimension`, `fontFamily`, `fontWeight`, `number`, `shadow`).
- Semantic leaves hold a reference string: `"{primitive.color.green.600}"`.
- Semantic names describe intent, not looks: `color.status.danger`, not `color.red`.

## Generated CSS
- `scripts/build-tokens.mjs` writes `src/styles/tokens.css`.
- Primitive path `primitive.color.green.600` → `--primitive-color-green-600`.
- Semantic path `semantic.color.text.muted` → `--color-text-muted: var(--primitive-color-slate-500)`.
- `tokens.css` is generated. Never edit it. Import it once, in the app entry and in `.storybook/preview.ts`.
- `tokens.css` is the one CSS file allowed raw values. A token-validator warning on it is expected.

## Component files
```
src/components/BudgetCard.tsx         # markup, props typed
src/components/BudgetCard.css         # var(--*) only
src/components/BudgetCard.test.tsx    # render + axe
src/components/BudgetCard.stories.tsx # one story per state
```

## Presentational contract
- Props are display-ready: strings already formatted, numbers already clamped.
- Variants are a typed union prop mapped to a `data-*` attribute.
- Callbacks are optional props (`onSelect?: () => void`). The component never decides what they do.
